<article class="env-corollary" id="01U6">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01U6">Corollary <span data-tag="01U6">5.1.3.9</span>.</a> Let $q: X \rightarrow S$ be an inner fibration of simplicial sets, let $z$ be a vertex of $X$, and let $e: s \rightarrow q(z)$ be an edge of $S$. Suppose that there exists a $q$-cartesian edge $g: y \rightarrow z$ of $X$ satisfying $q(g) = e$. Then any locally $q$-cartesian edge $h: x \rightarrow z$ satisfying $q(h) = e$ is $q$-cartesian. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="01TE" href="/tag/01TE">5.1.1.13</a>, we may assume without loss of generality that $S$ is an $\infty $-category (or even a simplex). Applying Remark <a data-tag="01U5" href="/tag/01U5">5.1.3.8</a>, we deduce that there is a $2$-simplex of $X$ as depicted in the diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  y \ar [dr]^{g} &amp;  \\ x \ar [ur]^{f} \ar [rr]^-{h} &amp;  &amp;  z, } \]
</div>
<p>
       where $f$ is an isomorphism in the $\infty $-category $X$. Then $f$ is also $q$-cartesian (Proposition <a data-tag="01TB" href="/tag/01TB">5.1.1.9</a>), so Corollary <a data-tag="01TS" href="/tag/01TS">5.1.2.4</a> guarantees that $h$ is $q$-cartesian. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
